1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:03,340
Listen up, everybody!

2
00:00:04,310 --> 00:00:09,680
If I die in this fight,
this guy is your new chief!

3
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:15,030
And I won't accept any objections,
protests, or other noise!

4
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,120
Come at me like you're gonna kill me!

5
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:23,620
Out of everyone I've ever fought before,
you're in the top grade.

6
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:29,040
Indeed. Very well. And if I die...

7
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:32,380
Yeah. I'll let your female go unharmed.

8
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,510
She's not "mine" yet.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,010
Hmph, you're really
making a bid for her, aren't you?

10
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:43,230
Is that plant monster 
really that fine a female?

11
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:45,100
Extremely so.

12
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:49,480
I'd like to see for myself.

13
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:52,320
If I win, I think I'll undress her
before returning her.

14
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:55,740
Then it seems I now have
an especially powerful reason not to lose.

15
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,240
You're really head-over-heels
for her, aren't you?

16
00:00:58,410 --> 00:01:00,840
Yeah, I'm head-over-heels.

17
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:05,540
Ha! Then beat me, and prove it!

18
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:07,670
That's what I intend to do.

19
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:50,210
Ha-ha, you survived that, huh?

20
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:52,480
You're a monk?

21
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:58,500
What's the matter? Aren't you going
to use that ability Frost Pain has?

22
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:03,010
Long ago, I was beaten
by the one who wielded it.

23
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:06,410
These are the wounds I received at the time.

24
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:10,900
If you activate it,
you might be able to beat me.

25
00:02:11,110 --> 00:02:13,980
Sorry, but I don't plan to use it.

26
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:16,530
Hmm, what are you, too stingy?

27
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:20,990
After you've exchanged blows with me,
do you still think I'm that way?

28
00:02:21,490 --> 00:02:25,990
No, you're not. Sorry, 
you didn't deserve that.

29
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:30,250
But if you aren't going to use it,
then here I come!

30
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:32,000
Iron Skin!

31
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:35,330
Damn it!

32
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:38,540
I've lost!

33
00:04:46,550 --> 00:04:47,720
Are you okay?

34
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:49,680
I'll cast some healing 
magic on you, right now.

35
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,610
Middle Cure Wounds.

36
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:57,980
Hey, now, you're making me jealous.

37
00:04:58,230 --> 00:05:00,850
Would you mind healing me, too, white stuff?

38
00:05:01,610 --> 00:05:02,650
Okay, okay.

39
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:07,950
It hurts quite a bit.
Feels like I got frozen to the bone.

40
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:11,370
Frost Pain carries a chill in its blade,

41
00:05:11,370 --> 00:05:15,370
and it delivers a little bit of
cold damage to those struck by it.

42
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:18,620
That's why you just
kept taking his attacks, right?

43
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,960
I thought that if you
didn't use that ability it has,

44
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:25,230
it would be just another cold sword.

45
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,760
Now that both of our wounds have been healed,

46
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:30,640
would it be okay if we got down to business?

47
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:35,390
Yeah! Or it <i>would</i> be, but first, drinks!

48
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:41,650
We can ease these annoying talks
with alcohol! You get me, right?

49
00:05:41,650 --> 00:05:43,400
No, I don't!

50
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:55,120
Hey, plant monster.

51
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,460
Have you finished talking?

52
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:01,090
Broadly speaking, yes.

53
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,290
So what are you going to do?

54
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,580
Huh?

55
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:07,880
We're gonna fight, of course!

56
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,800
You really are a fiend for fighting.

57
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,640
Don't flatter me; you'll make me blush.

58
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:15,270
So, can we win?

59
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:16,760
I don't know.

60
00:06:17,310 --> 00:06:21,770
Do you remember the words
of that monster that came as a herald?

61
00:06:22,310 --> 00:06:24,360
Sorry, I was asleep.

62
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:31,490
It said to us, "Offer a 
desperate resistance."

63
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:36,250
That's galling. They're looking down
on us right from the start.

64
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:39,370
That's right, our foe holds us
in complete contempt.

65
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:42,420
That's an indication of
how much force they must possess.

66
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:45,880
Which is why we're going to
obliterate their hubris.

67
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:47,880
Ha! Nice!

68
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:51,010
But even if we give
their pride a good thrashing,

69
00:06:51,010 --> 00:06:52,890
I don't think it gains us anything.

70
00:06:53,890 --> 00:06:58,390
I think I would prefer
holding on to life, even if it's in chains.

71
00:07:05,230 --> 00:07:07,050
I want you to listen to all this carefully.

72
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:12,870
If we're under their rule,
we may not even be able to do <i>this</i>.

73
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:16,170
But maybe we can. Isn't that right?

74
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:17,470
I'm not so sure.

75
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:22,920
I doubt that any being who would
watch on in enjoyment as we die

76
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,670
would have any mercy.

77
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:28,240
True enough. What I'm trying to say, though,

78
00:07:30,010 --> 00:07:31,220
is don't get killed.

79
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:34,680
I won't. Not until I hear your answer.

80
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:48,440
Ho, it's coming into sight.

81
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:53,450
Yeah, that's the Razor Tail village,
who they said would be first.

82
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:57,250
Those from the other villages
are probably already there.

83
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:03,560
This is all more than I can resist.

84
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,540
Welcome back, my little brother.

85
00:08:08,670 --> 00:08:13,220
Yeah. I've returned with good news, Brother.

86
00:08:13,470 --> 00:08:14,570
Hmm...

87
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:19,770
What's the deal with the plant monster?

88
00:08:19,770 --> 00:08:21,330
This is the female I love.

89
00:08:21,770 --> 00:08:23,020
With a mind toward marriage--

90
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:28,690
I see. So much for "I can't get married."

91
00:08:29,110 --> 00:08:31,640
You just didn't have anyone
you were in love with, right?

92
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:37,740
Now then, I am the chief of
the Green Claw tribe, Shasuryu Shasha.

93
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:41,620
Those we sent out as scouts 
have just returned.

94
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:44,190
Why don't we go listen 
to their detailed report?

95
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:48,000
The enemy's main stronghold is in the forest.

96
00:08:48,290 --> 00:08:51,170
They number just under around 5,000.

97
00:08:49,170 --> 00:08:55,760
"Small Fang Tribe"
"Chief Sukyu Juju"

98
00:08:51,170 --> 00:08:53,590
Their main force consist of
zombies and skeletons.

99
00:08:53,590 --> 00:08:57,260
We did not locate the one
who appears to be the army's leader.

100
00:08:57,260 --> 00:09:00,430
Hmm, our forces number roughly 1,300.

101
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:02,520
They outnumber us by over three to one.

102
00:09:02,810 --> 00:09:05,980
So we just have to take on
three or four of them each, right?

103
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,300
That's a cinch.

104
00:09:09,770 --> 00:09:12,570
First, we have to establish 
a chain of command.

105
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:15,530
Should we form brigades
centered around the chiefs?

106
00:09:15,530 --> 00:09:19,530
No, we should have a separate unit
consisting of only chiefs.

107
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:20,780
Hmm...?

108
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:24,790
Plan is to make... elite unit?

109
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:24,790
"Razor Tail Tribe"
"Chief Kyuku Zuzu"

110
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:27,210
That's right. The enemy's numbers are great.

111
00:09:27,670 --> 00:09:30,290
It may be necessary to go after their leader.

112
00:09:30,590 --> 00:09:32,170
And if there are any stronger foes,

113
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:34,760
we'll need to strike them
with smaller, elite forces.

114
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:38,050
But that will leave our side
without commanders, too, won't it?

115
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:41,260
All right, what if we have the separate unit

116
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:43,520
issue orders from the 
rear to the head hunters,

117
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:46,060
coordinating things as the situation demands?

118
00:09:48,650 --> 00:09:53,670
Four days until the enemy strikes.
We don't have a moment to waste.

119
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,790
Message.

120
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:11,790
Attention all forces. Advance!

121
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:19,050
Ah, so Cocytus has started 
advancing the army.

122
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:22,300
Yes. According to Entoma's message,

123
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:25,770
everything is <i>not</i> exceeding our expectations.

124
00:10:26,810 --> 00:10:31,480
As you ordered, Lord Ains,
Cocytus himself is not heading out,

125
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:34,150
and they are attacking with
only the forces they have been given.

126
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:38,650
I see. It's not exactly the outcome I wanted,

127
00:10:38,650 --> 00:10:41,320
but the question is, what 
will we get out of it?

128
00:10:53,090 --> 00:10:54,160
There they are.

129
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:01,740
Listen up, all of you Lizard Men!

130
00:11:02,470 --> 00:11:04,980
We recognize that the enemy is great!

131
00:11:05,930 --> 00:11:07,890
However, there is nothing to be afraid of!

132
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:13,360
For the first time in history,
our five tribes have formed an alliance!

133
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:17,480
It is through this alliance
that we have become one tribe,

134
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:21,410
and the ancestor spirits
of the five tribes will protect us all!

135
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:25,470
Let us defeat the enemy,
and offer victory to the ancestor spirits!

136
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:29,750
To war!

137
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,520
They're using the cavalry to get behind them,

138
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,570
surround them, and wipe them out, is that it?

139
00:11:56,940 --> 00:12:00,440
I think it's time for us
to make our first play, as well.

140
00:12:04,490 --> 00:12:05,820
Shoot them!

141
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:25,550
Are they thumbing their noses at us?

142
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:27,930
I can't seem to make sense of them.

143
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:30,950
Is it possible that they don't
have any commanders?

144
00:12:31,430 --> 00:12:35,140
So does that mean they think
they just needed greater numbers?

145
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:37,060
They're mocking us!

146
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:40,400
Still, we should reduce the enemy's numbers

147
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:42,190
as much as possible, while we can.

148
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:44,450
Tch, I wanna get out there, too!

149
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:47,410
Patience, Zenberu.

150
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:50,240
Just be patient
until the enemy's leader appears.

151
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:54,200
We can't afford to reveal the elite unit yet.

152
00:13:23,690 --> 00:13:28,290
I can't believe they can summon
Swamp Elementals in such a short time.

153
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:32,440
Working together really is an amazing thing.

154
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:39,170
Indeed. After that last war,
we did exchange small bits of information.

155
00:13:39,170 --> 00:13:43,760
After this incident is over,
there are more things I'd like to try.

156
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,680
Right, Zaryusu.

157
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:53,470
I underestimated the Lizard Men's morale.

158
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:57,210
Message.

159
00:13:58,150 --> 00:13:59,230
Demiurge...

160
00:14:00,810 --> 00:14:06,570
Yes, my friend. What in the world
has caused you to Message me?

161
00:14:06,570 --> 00:14:07,490
As it happens...

162
00:14:08,910 --> 00:14:13,370
I see. So what would you like me to do?

163
00:14:13,830 --> 00:14:19,000
I need some advice. If this defeat
is mine alone, I can accept it.

164
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:22,980
However, I can't do anything
to disgrace the Supreme One.

165
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:27,680
Does Lord Ains really want you to win?

166
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:30,010
What? What do you mean by that?

167
00:14:30,220 --> 00:14:36,180
I mean, why did Lord Ains
raise an army of such low-level servants?

168
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:37,270
Perhaps...

169
00:14:37,690 --> 00:14:40,190
Lord Ains wished for you 
to think for yourself,

170
00:14:40,190 --> 00:14:44,900
and gather some intelligence
to help you pursue victory?

171
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:48,340
It could be part of a plan
to promote your awareness.

172
00:14:48,990 --> 00:14:52,070
Additionally, the name of Nazarick
was never put forth.

173
00:14:52,070 --> 00:14:57,020
And you were forbidden to move on them,
as well. Which would mean...

174
00:14:58,250 --> 00:14:59,920
Hmm? Demiurge?

175
00:14:59,920 --> 00:15:04,210
Cocytus, I apologize,
but something has just come up.

176
00:15:04,210 --> 00:15:06,270
I wish you victory.

177
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:12,220
It's too late to do anything now, isn't it?

178
00:15:12,850 --> 00:15:15,770
Then there's no choice
but to send in the reserves.

179
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:22,190
I'm giving you an order, 
Elder Lich in command.

180
00:15:22,770 --> 00:15:26,690
Advance! Show the Lizard Men your power!

181
00:15:31,410 --> 00:15:34,660
Okay, carry the seriously
wounded to the village.

182
00:15:35,030 --> 00:15:37,910
The rest of you, follow us--

183
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:56,680
Run! That one isn't like
the other enemies up to now!

184
00:15:57,310 --> 00:16:01,020
You all head back and tell the chiefs
and Zaryusu about this!

185
00:16:01,690 --> 00:16:03,900
We'll buy you some time!

186
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:08,530
I, Iguva, will secure His victory.

187
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:25,500
It looks like we're up this time,
that's for sure.

188
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:30,170
Yeah, that's a powerful one.
Is that the army's commander?

189
00:16:30,170 --> 00:16:33,840
Even if it isn't, there's no doubt
he's their ace in reserve.

190
00:16:34,090 --> 00:16:38,220
Right. But how are we going to get near him?

191
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:41,660
It looks like he has a magic range
of about 100 meters.

192
00:16:47,310 --> 00:16:49,600
You're right. That's what we can do.

193
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:51,030
Zaryusu...?

194
00:16:56,990 --> 00:17:03,370
Fools. You think that slow-moving beast
can traverse this distance?!

195
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:13,800
Insufferable brute! Die!

196
00:17:21,850 --> 00:17:23,430
Why won't it stop?!

197
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,410
Why does it keep coming?!

198
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:32,770
Icy Burst!

199
00:17:37,450 --> 00:17:38,370
Wha--?

200
00:17:44,290 --> 00:17:45,510
Thanks, Rororo.

201
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,590
Impossible!

202
00:17:49,290 --> 00:17:51,110
Icy Burst!

203
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:56,970
Shoot as many as you like! 
I'll dispel them all!

204
00:17:57,300 --> 00:18:02,220
In that case, take my 
thunderbolts! Lightning!

205
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:05,040
Let me handle this.

206
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:10,400
Resistance... Massive!

207
00:18:10,690 --> 00:18:11,540
You saved us!

208
00:18:11,980 --> 00:18:13,780
Ha-ha, no sweat.

209
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:17,910
Summon Undead 4th!

210
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:26,540
I am Iguva, an Elder Lich
in the service of the Great One.

211
00:18:26,910 --> 00:18:30,920
If you bow your heads,
I will make your deaths painless.

212
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:33,640
In that case, here is your answer:

213
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:35,550
Hell no!

214
00:18:35,710 --> 00:18:39,640
Then realize that you have
rejected my final offer of mercy

215
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:43,560
as you suffer a death racked with anguish!

216
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:47,270
No, <i>you</i> go back to
the world of the dead, Iguva!

217
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:52,990
Forward, Zaryusu!

218
00:18:57,530 --> 00:19:00,360
Know terror! Scare!

219
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:06,010
Lion's Heart!

220
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:10,040
Zaryusu!

221
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:12,880
Pestiferous fool! Lightning!

222
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:15,830
Crusch!

223
00:19:18,010 --> 00:19:19,090
--Light--
--Too slow!

224
00:19:20,010 --> 00:19:21,550
Magic won't help you at this range!

225
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:25,100
Don't underestimate me, Lizard Man!

226
00:19:36,690 --> 00:19:42,880
Zaryusu, I'm finished here!
You take it... from... here...

227
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:52,880
Middle Cure Wounds!

228
00:19:57,550 --> 00:19:58,800
You won't best me!

229
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:03,590
I won't have you looking down on me!

230
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:05,600
Area-of-effect magic, at this range?

231
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:06,850
No!

232
00:20:06,890 --> 00:20:08,940
Icy Burst!

233
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:27,080
Hmph, you only hurt yourself,
not knowing that cold doesn't work on me.

234
00:20:28,910 --> 00:20:31,990
Now, where is he...?

235
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:46,680
I-I am a servant created by the One!

236
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:51,680
I will not be brought down...

237
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:55,390
...by something like this!

238
00:20:56,730 --> 00:21:00,150
Die, Lizard Man!

239
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:05,360
Rororo...

240
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,070
Zenberu...

241
00:21:07,990 --> 00:21:08,950
Crusch...

242
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:19,340
Impossible! How can you move?!

243
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:22,210
You monster!

244
00:21:22,210 --> 00:21:25,970
You're... finished!

245
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:34,350
Lord... Ains...

246
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:37,490
...forgive... me...

247
00:21:45,490 --> 00:21:49,200
Our gratitude to you!

248
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:54,340
Lord Cocytus,

249
00:21:54,750 --> 00:21:57,620
Lord Ains is calling for you.

250
00:21:59,290 --> 00:22:01,130
Understood.

